    "required_age": 0,
    "is_free": true,
    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\">In this free version of VRpatients, you\u2019ll care for sick patients and have the chance to practice fundamental clinical skills like listening to lung sounds on the Meta Quest or HTC VIVE headset. It\u2019s an engaging, hands-on\u00a0glimpse into\u00a0professional healthcare where anyone can learn essential skills and discover what it\u2019s really like to be a nurse or paramedic.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\">In this free version of VRpatients, you\u2019ll care for sick patients and have the chance to practice fundamental clinical skills like listening to lung sounds on the Meta Quest or HTC VIVE headset. It\u2019s an engaging, hands-on\u00a0glimpse into\u00a0professional healthcare where anyone can learn essential skills and discover what it\u2019s really like to be a nurse or paramedic.</p>",
    "short_description": "Step into VR/MR as a nurse or paramedic and experience safe, fun, and realistic healthcare scenarios\u2014no prior experience needed!",
    "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, French, German, Spanish - Latin America<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support",
    "reviews": "\u201cIf it didn\u2019t work for the students, then I wouldn\u2019t be as passionate about it, but the students like it. It gets them out of their seats and out from behind their computers and actively experiencing clinical scenarios in a safe, controlled environment. If I could do this every single day, I would because I really think it\u2019s an amazing way for them to learn.\u201d<br />\r\nUniversity of Cincinnati<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u201cIt\u2019s a safe place for students to \u2018crash and burn\u2019 and it sounds awful, but we\u2019d much rather you kill a simulative patient than a real one.\u201d<br />\r\n HealthONE<br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u201cWe are using VRpatients to meet our students where they\u2019re at so we can get them immersed with hands on learning as soon as they walk in the door and and ultimately, patients will get better care..\u201d<br />\r\nGreenville Technical College<br />\r\n",
